.TH MACOSX-CROSS-CLANG 1 "September 2026" "macosx-cross @MACOSX_CROSS_VERSION@" "macosx-cross"
.SH NAME
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ \- macOS cross-compiling @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@ wrapper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@-options ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@
is a @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@ wrapper provided by
.BR macosx-cross (1)
for cross-compiling software for Apple platforms from a non-macOS host.

The wrapper selects the requested macOS SDK, configures the appropriate
Apple target and sysroot, and invokes
.BR @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ (1)
with the LLVM LLD linker.

The SDK must have been installed and initialized by
.BR macosx-cross .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --macosx-cross-path
Print the macosx-cross installation directory and exit.

.TP
.BI --macosx-sdk=VERSION
Select the macOS SDK version.

.TP
.BI --macosx-sdk " VERSION"
Select the macOS SDK version.

.TP
.BI --target=TARGET
Select the Apple target triple.

.TP
.BI --target " TARGET"
Select the Apple target triple.

.SH TARGETS
Targets are obtained from the SDK metadata.

For macOS targets, the target has the form:

.PP
.EX
ARCH-apple-darwin
.EE

For iOS targets:

.PP
.EX
ARCH-apple-ios
.EE

For iOS Simulator / Mac Catalyst targets:

.PP
.EX
ARCH-apple-ios-macabi
.EE

Only architectures supported by the selected SDK are accepted.

.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MACOSX_SDK_VERSION
Default SDK version when
.B --macosx-sdk
is not specified.

.TP
.B MACOSX_TARGET
Default target triple when
.B --target
is not specified.

.TP
.B MACOSX_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target used for macOS builds.

If unset, it defaults to the selected SDK version.

.TP
.B IPHONEOS_DEPLOYMENT_TARGET
Deployment target used for iOS and Mac Catalyst builds.

If unset, it defaults to the selected SDK version.

.TP
.B SYSTEM_FRAMEWORK_SEARCH_PATHS
Additional system framework search path.

The value is passed to @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@ using the
.B -F
option.

.TP
.B FRAMEWORK_SEARCH_PATHS
Framework search path passed to @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@ using the
.B -F
option.

.TP
.B KASAN_DEFAULT_CFLAGS
Default CFLAGS used by the wrapper when KASAN flags are configured.

.TP
.B KASAN_DEFAULT_CFLAGS_ARM64
Default CFLAGS used for
.B arm64
and
.B arm64e
targets when configured.

.SH CLANG
After processing its own options,
.B macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@
passes all remaining arguments directly to
.BR @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ (1).

The wrapper invokes @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@ with options equivalent to:

.PP
.EX
@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ \\
    --target=TARGET \\
    --sysroot=SDK \\
    -fuse-ld=lld \\
    -Wno-unused-command-line-argument
.EE

Additional framework search paths and configured default CFLAGS are also
passed when available.

.SH EXAMPLES
Compile a C source file for macOS:

.PP
.EX
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ \\
    --macosx-sdk 14.5 \\
    --target x86_64-apple-darwin \\
    -c hello.@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_FILE@ \\
    -o hello.o
.EE

.PP
Compile for Apple Silicon:

.PP
.EX
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ \\
    --macosx-sdk 14.5 \\
    --target arm64-apple-darwin \\
    -c hello.@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_FILE@ \\
    -o hello.o
.EE

.PP
Compile and link:

.PP
.EX
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ \\
    --macosx-sdk 14.5 \\
    --target arm64-apple-darwin \\
    hello.@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_FILE@ \\
    -o hello
.EE

.PP
Use environment variables instead of command-line options:

.PP
.EX
MACOSX_SDK_VERSION=14.5 \\
MACOSX_TARGET=arm64-apple-darwin \\
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ hello.@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_FILE@ -o hello
.EE

.PP
Display the macosx-cross installation path:

.PP
.EX
macosx-cross-@MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ --macosx-cross-path
.EE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/
macosx-cross installation directory.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/
Installed macOS SDK directory.

.TP
.I @MACOSX_CROSS_LIBDIR@/MacOSX.sdk/VERSION/.metadata
Metadata for an installed SDK.

.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Successful execution.

.TP
.B non-zero
An error occurred, the requested SDK or target is invalid, or @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG_TEXT@
returned an error.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR @MACOSX_CROSS_CLANG@ (1),
.BR lld (1),
.BR macosx-cross (1)

